HTTP and TLS are the technologies used to communicate securely the information between the client and the server

http hypertext transfer protocol defines how the browser and client send requests and responses
tls(transport layer security):
this encrypts the communication between them by encrypting the data

http is not secured and the attackers may tamper or stole the data
where in https TLS is used to encrypt the data

http uses the port 80
and https uses port 443

When we send a request using HTTPS, TLS generally works as:

Client Hello: The browser proposes TLS versions and cryptographic options.

Server authentication: The server presents its digital certificate.

Key establishment: The browser and server establish shared session keys.

Secure communication: HTTP requests and responses are encrypted using those keys.

the intial negotiation is known as tls handshake

